# 1. Two Sum

**Link:** https://leetcode.com/problems/two-sum/
**Difficulty:** Easy
**Topics:** Array, Hash Map

## Problem
Given an array of integers `nums` and an integer `target`, return the indices of the two numbers that add up to `target`. Each input has exactly one solution, and you may not use the same element twice.

## Approach
Use a hash map to store each number's value and index as we iterate. For every number, check if `target - number` already exists in the map. If it does, we've found our pair. This avoids the need for a nested loop.

## Complexity
- **Time:** O(n) - single pass through the array
- **Space:** O(n) - hash map can store up to n elements

## Notes
Brute force would be O(n²) by checking every pair. The hash map trade-off (extra space for speed) is a common pattern in array problems - keep this technique in mind for similar "find a pair/triplet" questions.
